@startuml analyse-parcours-dispatch-activite
title DISPATCH mechanism — Flow of the journey analysis waves

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
  DiamondBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  DiamondBorderColor #5BA1BC
}
skinparam ArrowColor #5BA1BC
skinparam ActivityBarColor #5BA1BC
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9BD0DD
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #ECECF2
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #5BA1BC

|#E0F0F4| Main context |
start

:SKILL.md -> reads 25_dispatch-orchestration.md;

note right
  Platform detection:
  - Claude Code -> isolated sub-agents (parallel)
  - Others -> sequential inline execution
end note

partition "**Wave 0 — Location** (main context)" {
  :Read args: directory or direct files;
  :Identify .har + Coverage-*.json + cwv.json (optional);
  :Check HAR existence + size\n(selective reading if > 5 MB);
}

note right #C8E6C9
  ✅ Wave 0 done — files ready
  The following dispatches read the disk files.
end note

partition "**Wave 1 — HAR + Coverage + CWV + env-data + Security** (5 sub-agents in parallel)" {
  fork
    :Dispatch analyze-har
    (20_har-analysis.md)
    python3 analyze_har.py <source-dir>
    Traffic + performance (requests, domains,
    HTTP codes, duplicates, blocking resources)
    -> har-analysis.json;
  fork again
    :Dispatch analyze-coverage
    (30_coverage-analysis.md)
    Format A or B detected
    JS/CSS metrics per page
    (total KB, unused KB, %)
    Top 5 unused JS + Top 3 unused CSS
    Multi-page summary + outliers
    -> coverage-analysis.json;
  fork again
    :Dispatch collect-cwv
    (37_lighthouse.md)
    collect_cwv_pagespeed.py --strategy both
    PageSpeed Insights + CrUX (mobile+desktop,
    accessibility/best-practices included from the
    start) ; automatic Lighthouse fallback if
    GOOGLE_API_KEY absent or 0 usable metric
    -> cwv.json;
  fork again
    :Dispatch collect-env-data
    (45_efootprint.md, Step 20)
    collect_env_data.py <source-dir>
    HAR + CrUX (device mix) + ipinfo.io
    (country/provider) + internal SimilarWeb API
    (country mix + traffic)
    -> env-data.json;
  fork again
    :Dispatch extractor-security-headers
    (39_eof-audit.md)
    analyze_security_headers.py <source-dir>
    Local security score from the headers
    already in the .har, no network call
    -> security-headers-analysis.json;
  end fork
}

note right
  Independence verified in code, not assumed:
  analyze-har and extractor-security-headers ALSO
  read env-data.json, but in SOFT degradation
  (file absent -> less precise classification /
  page filter ignored, never a crash).
  Success condition:
  har-analysis.json AND coverage-analysis.json
  mandatory (blocking warning if absent).
  cwv.json / env-data.json / security-headers-analysis.json
  best-effort (absence signaled, never blocking).
end note

partition "**Wave 2 — EOF extractors depending on env-data.json** (2 sub-agents in parallel)" {
  fork
    :Dispatch extractor-html-css
    depends_on="collect-env-data"
    parse_html_criteria.py <source-dir>
    Live re-fetch of already audited pages
    (the .har does not contain the HTML/CSS bodies)
    Archived under html-pages/ (job 27)
    -> html-css-criteria.json;
  fork again
    :Dispatch extractor-wellknown
    depends_on="collect-env-data"
    scan_wellknown.py <source-dir>
    Direct fetch security.txt / robots.txt /
    sitemap.xml on the domain deduced from env-data.json
    -> wellknown-scan.json;
  end fork
}

note right #FFECB3
  HARD DEPENDENCY (not a degradation), verified
  line by line in the code:
  parse_html_criteria.py and scan_wellknown.py
  sys.exit(1) if env-data.json is absent or empty.
  Never dispatch this wave before having
  confirmed env-data.json on disk (Wave 1 done) —
  a simple retry does not compensate for this hard dependency.
end note

partition "**Merge + rest** (main context)" {
  :Read har-analysis.json + coverage-analysis.json
  (mandatory) + cwv.json / env-data.json /
  security-headers-analysis.json / html-css-criteria.json /
  wellknown-scan.json (best-effort, Wave 1/2);
  :Step 35 — har_metrics.py
  Score/grade A-G per page calculation
  (official cnumr/ecoindex formula);

  note right
    Limits:
    DOM=0 if HAR without HTML body
    SPA: DOM = initial state only
    -> documented in the report
    No OUTPUT_FILE reused elsewhere:
    free console validation, outside dispatch
  end note

  note right #FFECB3
    If cwv.json absent (Wave 1 failed):
    report without CWV, HAR onLoad used
    as LCP proxy
  end note

  :Step 39 — run_eof.py <source-dir>
  Confronts har-analysis.json / coverage-analysis.json
  (mandatory) + cwv.json / env-data.json /
  security-headers-analysis.json / html-css-criteria.json /
  wellknown-scan.json (best-effort, already produced by
  Wave 1/2 — no more annex extractors to launch here)
  against eof-reference.json (54 criteria + 16 quick diagnostic)
  -> eof-audit-results.json, eof-filled.md,
  eof-radar-<domain>.svg;

  note right #FFECB3
    STOP HERE, nothing is automatic after:
    generate_questionnaire.py / parse_questionnaire.py /
    merge_lots.py are manual steps taken on purpose
    (mission decision), never triggered by this skill.
    Trap: never rerun run_eof.py alone after a
    questionnaire read-back (it silently overwrites the answers,
    it never re-reads lots/questionnaire-review.json).
    Always parse_questionnaire.py -> merge_lots.py
    -> generate_report_html.py.
  end note

  :Step 40 — generate_report_html.py
  Sections: Recommendations P1/P2/P3,
  GreenIT best practices, CWV (if cwv.json),
  e-footprint CO2e (if efootprint-python-summary.json),
  EOF optimization potential (if eof-audit-results.json,
  measured + questionnaire merged),
  Appendices (EcoIndex, Traffic, Dead code)
  -> journey-report-YYYY-MM-DD.html
  (internal check_report_values.py, non-blocking);

  :deliver the report path to the user;

  note right #E0F0F4
    Conditional CO2e section:
    displayed only if efootprint-python-summary.json
    is present in the audit-dir
  end note
}

partition "**Optional step - e-footprint CO2e** (skill /efootprint)" #C8E6C9 {
  if (User launches /efootprint ?) then (yes)
    :E1 - collect_env_data.py
    HAR extraction (weight, duration, IP)
    API ipinfo.io (country + provider)
    CrUX (desktop/mobile device mix)
    -> env-data.json;

    note right
      Cache mode:
      If env-data.json already exists (often already
      produced by the Wave 1 of /analyse-parcours,
      collect-env-data block), skip API calls
      (except --refresh)
    end note

    :E2 - AskUserQuestion
    - Annual traffic (visits/year) [REQUIRED]
    - Cloud instance (if AWS/Azure/GCP detected);

    :E3 - run_efootprint.py
    Boavizta model (devices/network/server/storage)
    Manufacturing + energy calculation
    -> efootprint-boavizta-model.json
    -> efootprint-python-summary.json;

    note right
      Results:
      - Total CO2e (kg/year)
      - Per visit (g CO2e/visit)
      - Manufacturing/energy breakdown
      - Hypotheses + confidence badges
    end note

    :E4 - Regenerate HTML report
    generate_report_html.py
    -> report enriched with the CO2e section;

    :CO2e impact summary
    delivered to the user;
  else (no)
    :Report without CO2e section;
  endif
}

stop

@enduml
